; smoke.grid - cmd.exe printing its banner and a prompt.
; Audited by hand against corpus/smoke.bin, every one of its 316 bytes: the banner text, the OSC 0
; title, the CUP to row 4, the 136-character prompt wrapping at column 120, and the final ?25h.
; No divergent path is exercised - the corpus contains no truecolor, no SGR 9, no wide character,
; no private-parameter CSI u, no multi-parameter DEC private mode and no mode 2026.
;
; Ported to the unified seam. The header key that lists wrapped rows is now 'continues', and
; ITerminalGrid.ContinuesPreviousRow(N) is true for the row that continues the one above it -
; the direction the engine already stores, and the only direction that is answerable for the
; bottom viewport row. The rows listed are exactly the ones this file has always listed, so the
; audited wrap points are unchanged; the key was renamed so that a file written under the
; earlier 'wrapped' key cannot be mistaken for one written under this one.
;
; Corrected 2026-08-28: the title and icon read WINDOWS\\YSTEM32 here, which was the
; engine's output and not the corpus. The recording sends OSC 0 over bytes 75..106 and the
; third frame boundary falls at byte 90, on the 'S' of SYSTEM32; XtermSharp's OscPut drops the
; first byte of the payload run that follows a feed boundary. The bytes say SYSTEM32, so the
; golden says SYSTEM32 and the replay of this corpus is red until that parser is fixed.
;
; Corrected 2026-08-28: every cursor line here read 'steady', which was the engine reporting a
; TerminalOptions field nothing ever wrote (gap 11) and not audited terminal behaviour. The
; power-on cursor style is a blinking block - DECSCUSR Ps=0 and Ps=1 both name it as the default -
; and corpus/smoke.bin contains no DECSCUSR and no DEC mode 12, so the cursor blinks for the whole
; of this recording. All seven frames now read 'blink'.
;
# smoke  frame 1/7  after 45/316 bytes  (interval sample)
size 120x30
alt off
cursor col=13 row=0 hidden shape=block blink
scrollback 0
title ""
icon ""
modes autowrap focus mouse=off/x10 kitty=none
continues none
text
  r00 |Microsoft Win|
  r01-r29 ~blank~
style
  s00-s29 ~default~
legend
    .  default

